# the mink library, what a dependent's `use mink;` binds
#
# each module forwarded here is the public surface, and every other module of
# src is internal to mink and may change without notice: the format
# internals, the relocation rows and the link phases. a pair's relocation
# kinds are public, as a producer names them in static tables, while the rows
# that apply them are not. the registry is the route to files, models,
# relocation rows and trait encodings. a dependent imports only through this
# list by practice and review holds the line, as nothing in the build marks
# or enforces it. a change to a module on the list carries a Consumer changes
# section naming its downstream port.

# the startup a test dispatcher of this library links
use std.runtime;
# modules no forwarded module reaches, whose tests run with the library's
use mink.format.coff.import.implib;
use mink.format.elf.rules.linked;

